{
  "id": "agentMemoryProvenance",
  "name": "Trace, correct and forget: memory provenance (Redis Agent Memory)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Why does the agent believe that?\n\nCorrections (\"I moved from Berlin to Madrid\"), audit (\"which conversation produced this?\") and memory poisoning are rising concerns in the n8n forum and in Mem0's issue tracker, and no other n8n memory node shows where a memory came from. Every memory here carries its **sources**: the session and the exact events it was extracted from.\n\nThree small HTTP endpoints an operator or an admin workflow can call:\n\n**Trace** — `POST /webhook/memory/trace` `{ \"userId\": \"demo-user\", \"query\": \"where does the user live\" }`\nSearch with *Include Sources* → **Session → Get**. The reply lists each memory with the messages that produced it. A memory created directly (by a Save tool, say) has no sources and is reported as such.\n\n**Correct** — `POST /webhook/memory/correct` `{ \"userId\": \"demo-user\", \"query\": \"where does the user live\", \"text\": \"The user lives in Madrid.\" }`\nFinds the user's memory closest to the query (or to the new text, when no query is given) and rewrites it in place.\n\n**Forget a thread** — `POST /webhook/memory/forget-thread` `{ \"userId\": \"demo-user\", \"sessionId\": \"…\" }`\nDeletes the session and every memory extracted from it: the fix for a conversation that came from an untrusted channel. Without `sessionId`, the user's most recent session goes.\n\nSelect your **Redis Agent Memory API** credential on every Redis node. Seed memories first by chatting with another example in this folder as `demo-user`; extraction takes up to a minute or two.\n\n**Try it in the editor.** Each webhook carries a pinned sample request for `demo-user`, so no client is needed: open **Respond with the report**, **Respond with the memory** or **Respond: thread forgotten** and choose **Execute step**. Pinned data applies to editor runs only; a live `POST` is used as is.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 500
      },
      "id": "sticky-note",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -840,
        -300
      ]
    },
